{"parentUuid":"8c752fa9-5d11-4a57-812d-a87bceef47f1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwurvPw5vj1GJtLbX1L3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_read_input_tokens":540496,"output_tokens":1161,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":45},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input_tokens":540496,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"e6e26f5f-905e-4e53-bd41-796aa0fce521","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgwurupwiVKg1nkYd3CWH","type":"assistant","uuid":"034a21d3-7d86-46c0-ad37-fc6c934d40ad","timestamp":"2026-11-11T22:15:17.643Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","session_id":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/tacoda/tacoda/bastion","sessionId":"4fe51ecd-d6cc-423f-a39e-68f5e5b7e45e","version":"2.1.285","gitBranch":"main","slug":"parsed-tinkering-blum"}
{"parentUuid":"034a21d3-7d86-46c0-ad37-fc6c934d40ad","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgwurvPw5vj1GJtLbX1L3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The sidebar is gone. A bar across the top now holds the castle, the pages, and a server switcher, and Jobs, Audit Log and Costs can show all servers at once. Each phase was checked live in the app with a second server (`two`) added. All CI steps and the CodeScene safeguard pass. There are four commits (`93dbbea`, `086bbe7`, `9dbee06`, `45c6495`), not pushed.\n\n**U1, the top bar**\n- The bar shows the castle, the ten pages with the count of jobs that wait, and the switcher.\n- The switcher is one button per server, each with a dot for its connection. On Jobs, Audit Log and Costs it also offers \"All servers\".\n- The other pages (Workflows, Constraints and so on) show one server only. If \"All servers\" is on when you open one, it shows the last server you picked.\n- The Jobs page follows the switcher, so its own server filter is gone.\n\n**U2, records across servers**\n- Costs adds up by server, workspace, step and day. When several servers show, each workspace is named with its server.\n- The Audit Log is now its own page. It shows each server's chain and check, and every entry in one list, newest first.\n- Export writes the file on the server, so it works only when one server is picked.\n- Fixed: a records page you just opened read only one server, because it read under the page you came from.\n\n**U3, charts**\n- One stacked bar chart covers the last 30 days. Hovering a bar names the day and each part. Live, 11-06 read $0.0658: local $0.0628 and two $0.0029, the same as the table.\n- Costs splits spend by server. Jobs splits the jobs started each day by how they ended. The Audit Log splits entries by kind.\n- Jobs, the Audit Log and Verification also show number tiles.\n- The audit chart covers only the newest 200 entries per server, the most the server sends at once, so today it shows only today. Its title says so.\n\n**U4, cleaner pages**\n- Every page has the same head: the title, one line on what it shows and on which server, and its actions on the right.\n- An error line appears only when there is an error, so empty ones no longer leave gaps.\n- A job's title is the first line of its request, with the full request under it.\n- Text that still mentioned stages, pipelines or \"stop at review\" is rewritten.\n- At the smallest window size (720×480), the bar wraps to two rows and nothing is cut off.\n\n**Things to know**\n- **Exemption:** iced's chart drawing code needs more function arguments than CodeScene allows. The repo already exempted `drawing.rs` for the same reason, so I added `chart.rs` to `.codescene/code-health-rules.json`.\n- **Still running:** my dev server `two` on port 49191 and the dev desktop app. `two` is now saved in your server list. I put its token on the clipboard, pasted it into Settings without reading it, and then cleared the clipboard.\n- **Pointer file:** `~/Library/Application Support/dev.tacoda.bastion/local-server` pointed to an old data folder. I changed it to the folder the running server uses.\n\n**Queued in PLAN.md**\n1. Step names as `workflow/step`, with constraints and capabilities set per workflow step.\n2. A model choice on each step.\n3. Workflows that branch on failure, drawn as flowcharts.\n\nItem 1 changes D42 and the gate.\n\nShould I push these four commits?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":437,"cache_read_input_tokens":540496,"output_tokens":1161,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":45},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":437,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1161,"cache_read_input